course: dictionary
lesson: 14314
title: Objective: a goal or a fair view
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Objective has more than one meaning, so context helps you pick the right one. Look at the words around it. «Our objective today is to learn how to multiply fractions.» The words "today" and "learn" show that objective means a goal, something you are trying to reach.
explain: As an adjective, objective means fair and based on facts, not on feelings. «The judge must stay objective and ignore whether she likes the player.» The clue is "ignore whether she likes": objective means judging by facts, not by personal opinion.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Write what you measured, not what you hoped: be objective.» Put in "based on facts, not hopes" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Objective (noun) means an aim or goal you are trying to reach, such as a learning objective.
fact: Objective (adjective) means based on facts and not on personal feelings or opinions.
fact: Objective can also mean real and able to be measured or checked.
fact: In science, the objective is the lens nearest the object in a microscope.
fact: Useful phrases: learning objective, main objective, stay objective.
exercise: «Today's objective is to add fractions.» What does objective mean here? | * A goal you are trying to reach | A lens in a microscope | A feeling of being sad | A type of fraction
exercise: «The referee was objective and judged only by the rules.» What does objective mean here? | Lost in the game | * Based on facts, not personal feelings | Very angry with the players | Loud and cheerful
exercise: «Her main objective was to finish the race.» Find and copy the word that means a goal you are trying to reach. | * objective | race | main | finish
test: «Write what you saw, not what you hoped. Be objective.» What does objective mean in this sentence? | * Based on facts, not hopes | Full of wishes and dreams | Written in a secret code | Written in red ink
test: In a microscope, what is the objective? | * The lens nearest the object you are looking at | The eyepiece you look through | The stand that holds the slide | The light at the bottom
exam: Which sentence uses objective to mean a goal? | She stayed objective when she judged the poem. | The rules were objective and fair. | * Our class objective this week is to read ten pages a day. | The scientist wrote an objective report.
